{{!
    Was a ContentPanel wrapping a raw <table>: px-4 py-3 cells, nine columns all
    always visible, and no search, sorting, pagination or column picker. The New
    Adjustment button was passed as a block to Layout::Section::Header alongside a
    sentence of description — that block renders inside the actions wormhole, so
    the description was sitting where the buttons go. The button is a proper
    @onPressNew now and the description is gone, as on the other lists.
}}
<Layout::Resource::Tabular
    @title={{t "inventory.screens.adjustments-list"}}
    @searchQuery={{this.query}}
    @onSearch={{perform this.search}}
    @data={{@model}}
    @columns={{this.columns}}
    @page={{this.page}}
    @onPageChange={{fn (mut this.page)}}
    @setupTable={{fn (mut this.table)}}
    @controller={{this}}
    @onPressNew={{this.createAdjustment}}
/>
{{outlet}}